(LangGraph: Graphs for Language Model Applications) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(LangGraph is a library for building language model applications as graphs. An) Tj T*
(application is defined by a state object, a set of nodes, and a set of edges. Each node) Tj T*
(is a function that reads the state and returns an update to it. Each edge says which) Tj T*
(node runs next. The graph runs node by node until it reaches a terminal node.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(State is usually a TypedDict, which is a dictionary type where each key has a declared) Tj T*
(type. Nodes receive the whole state and return only the fields they change; the) Tj T*
(framework merges those updates into the state. This makes the flow of information) Tj T*
(explicit: to understand what a node can see, read the state definition, not the node) Tj T*
(code alone.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Edges come in two kinds. A normal edge always goes from one node to another. A) Tj T*
(conditional edge calls a routing function that looks at the state and returns the name) Tj T*
(of the next node. Conditional edges are how a graph branches: for example, a planner) Tj T*
(node may route to a retriever node when documents are needed and to a direct-answer node) Tj T*
(when they are not.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cycles are allowed. A graph may loop back to an earlier node, for example to retry a) Tj T*
(failed retrieval with a rewritten query or to regenerate an answer that failed) Tj T*
(verification. A loop must have a termination condition, such as a retry counter stored) Tj T*
(in state that stops the loop after one retry. Without a cap, a graph can loop forever on) Tj T*
(a question it cannot answer.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(LangGraph also supports persistence through checkpointers. A checkpointer saves the) Tj T*
(graph state after each step, so a run can be resumed after a failure. Checkpointers also) Tj T*
(enable human-in-the-loop workflows: a graph can pause before a sensitive step, wait for) Tj T*
(a human to approve or edit the state, and then continue from the checkpoint. Interrupts) Tj T*
(are declared on specific nodes, not added as ad-hoc pauses in node code.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Streaming in LangGraph works by running the graph and yielding events as nodes produce) Tj T*
(them, rather than waiting for the whole run to finish. Token streaming from a language) Tj T*
(model node is one kind of event; status events from other nodes are another. A client) Tj T*
(that ignores unknown event types keeps working when new status events are added later.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
